Verify that a Dockerfile exists in the repository and that Jenkins checks out the correct branch. If the Dockerfile is in a subfolder, specify the path in the Docker build command. Example Jenkinsfile snippet:
```groovy
pipeline {
    agent any
    stages {
        stage('Build Docker') {
            steps {
                sh 'docker build -t myapp:${BUILD_NUMBER} ./path/to/docker'
            }
        }
    }
}
```

```groovy
pipeline {
    agent any
    triggers {
        pollSCM('H/5 * * * *')
    }
    stages {
        stage('Deploy') {
            when {
                branch 'master'
            }
            steps {
                sh './deploy.sh'
            }
        }
    }
}
```
